1️⃣ LeetCode #33 — Search in Rotated Sorted Array

Medium

class Solution {
    public int search(int[] nums, int target) {
        int left = 0;
        int right = nums.length - 1;

        while (left <= right) {
            int mid = left + (right - left) / 2;

            if (nums[mid] == target) {
                return mid;
            }

            // Left half is sorted
            if (nums[left] <= nums[mid]) {
                if (nums[left] <= target && target < nums[mid]) {
                    right = mid - 1;
                } else {
                    left = mid + 1;
                }
            }
            // Right half is sorted
            else {
                if (nums[mid] < target && target <= nums[right]) {
                    left = mid + 1;
                } else {
                    right = mid - 1;
                }
            }
        }

        return -1;
    }
}

🧠 Core idea: Every step-la one half definitely sorted. Sorted half-kulla target irukka-nu check panni search space reduce pannuvom.

Time: O(log n)
Space: O(1)

2️⃣ LeetCode #153 — Find Minimum in Rotated Sorted Array

Medium

class Solution {
    public int findMin(int[] nums) {
        int left = 0;
        int right = nums.length - 1;

        while (left < right) {
            int mid = left + (right - left) / 2;

            if (nums[mid] > nums[right]) {
                left = mid + 1;
            } else {
                right = mid;
            }
        }

        return nums[left];
    }
}
🧠 Simple logic

nums[mid] > nums[right]

➡️ Minimum right side-la irukkum.

Otherwise:

➡️ Minimum left side including mid-la irukkum.

Example:

[4,5,6,7,0,1,2]

➡️ Answer = 0

Time: O(log n)
Space: O(1)

3️⃣ LeetCode #875 — Koko Eating Bananas

Medium

class Solution {
    public int minEatingSpeed(int[] piles, int h) {
        int left = 1;
        int right = 0;

        for (int pile : piles) {
            right = Math.max(right, pile);
        }

        while (left < right) {
            int mid = left + (right - left) / 2;

            long hours = 0;

            for (int pile : piles) {
                hours += (pile + mid - 1) / mid;
            }

            if (hours <= h) {
                right = mid;
            } else {
                left = mid + 1;
            }
        }

        return left;
    }
}
